$DATUM Cobalt-Catalyzed Reaction of 18 with p-Methoxystyrene (eq 10) Anhydrous
cobalt(II) chloride (46 mg, 0.35 mmol) and DPPH (195 mg, 0.43 mmol) were
stirred in diethyl ether (10 mL) at room temperature for 30 min under an
atmosphere of argon. The bromide 18 (1.5 g, 3.6 mmol) in diethyl ether (5
mL), p-methoxystyrene (0.49 g, 3.6 mmol), and
trimethylsilylmethylmagnesium chloride (2 M in diethyl ether, 5.4 mL, 10
mmol) were then added dropwise to the [CoCl2(dpph)] complex sequentially.
The resultant mixture was then heated at reflux for 6 h, after which it
was allowed to cool and then poured into a saturated solution of aqueous
ammonium chloride (20 mL). Extractive workup followed by purification on
silica gel with 5% diethyl ether in hexane as eluent gave the olefins
trans-19 and cis-19 (1.4 g, 2.9 mmol, 82%), a colorless oil, in a ratio
of 64:36. t-Butyldiphenylsilyl
trans-2-[(E)-2-(p-methoxyphenyl)ethenyl]cyclohexyl ether (19), yield 1.4
g, 2.9 mmol, 82% IR (neat) 2929, 1608, 1510, 1463, 1472, 1247, 1110,
1080, 1037, 823, 702 cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz) δ 1.00 (s, 0.36 × 9H,
for cis isomer), 1.08 (s, 0.64 × 9H, for trans isomer), 1.10-1.93 (m,
7H), 2.18-2.26 (m, 1H), 3.45-3.51 (m, 1H), 3.82 (s, 3H), 3.96-3.99 (m,
1H), 5.95 (dd, J = 16.5, 7.5 Hz, 0.36 × 1H, for cis isomer), 6.20 (dd, J
= 15.5, 6.5 Hz, 0.64 × 1H, for trans isomer), 6.24 (d, J= 16.5 Hz, 0.36 ×
1H, for cis isomer), 6.27 (d, J= 15.5 Hz, 0.64 × 1H, for trans isomer),
6.80-6.83 (m, 2H), 7.12-7.17 (m, 2H), 7.24-7.34 (m, 4H), 7.36-7.41 (m,
2H), 7.64-7.67 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125.6 MHz, some signals overlap)
δ 19.3, 19.5, 24.6, 24.8, 27.1, 27.2, 27.3, 31.0, 32.8, 35.3, 46.3, 49.3,
55.3, 72.6, 75.9, 113.8, 127.4, 127.5, 128.6, 128.7, 129.1, 129.3, 129.4,
130.9, 131.0, 131.7, 132.0, 132.8, 132.9, 134.4, 134.7, 135.2, 136.1,
136.2, 158.5. Found: C, 78.86; H, 8.27%. Calcd for C31H38O2Si: C, 79.10;
H, 8.14%.
