$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
Dimethyl 10b-methyl-3,10b-dihydrofluoranthene-2,2(1H)-dicarboxylate (6).
The reaction mixture was chromatographed using 15:1 hexane/EtOAc to
afford 75 mg of the indicated compound (82 % yield) as a colorless oil:
1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.06 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H), 1.33 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 1.89
(d, J = 14.7 Hz, 1H), 3.09 (d, J = 14.7 Hz, 1H), 3.47 (d, J = 1.2 Hz,
2H), 3.90-4.00 (m, 2H), 4.32 (dq, J = 1.2, 7.2 Hz, 2H), 7.15 (d, J = 7.5
Hz, 1H), 7.25-7.37 (m, 3H), 7.48-7.51 (m, 1H), 7.56 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H),
7.70-7.72 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.0, 14.3, 24.3, 33.3, 38.6, 46.2,
56.6, 61.7, 62.0, 118.8, 121.0, 123.4, 126.0, 127.3, 127.5, 128.0, 132.6,
138.2, 140.2, 149.4, 154.4, 172.0, 172.9; IR (neat, cm-1) 2978, 2930,
1732, 1446; HRMS Calcd for C23H24O4: 364.1674. Found: 364.1684.
