$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM iv) Procedures for one –pot synthesis of product 2a: 0.3 mmol (1 equiv)
of enamide was dissolved in 1 mL of anhydrous DMF in a screw cap via
under argon atmosphere. The solution was cooled to 0 °C and 0.45 mmol
(1.5 equiv) of sodium hydride (60% dispersion in mineral oil) was added
in portions. The resulting suspension was stirred at the same temperature
for 10 min. Benzyl bromide (0.6 mmol, 2 equiv) was then added dropwise.
The final solution was warmed to room temperature and continued to stir
for 12 hours. Then palladium (II)acetate (6.8 mg, 0.03 mmol, 10 mol%),
triphenylphosphine (15.8 mg, 0.06 mmol, 20 mol%), triethylamine (60.7 mg,
0.6 mmol, 2.0 equiv) and 4 mL DMF were added into the mixture. The vial
was heated at 120 °C for 24 hours. The solution was cooled to room
temperature and diluted with ethylacetate, washed with saturated ammonium
chloride solution. The organic layer was concentrated under vacuum and
the product was isolated through flash column chromatography
(hexane/ethylacetate). The corresponding product. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.37-7.10 (m, 9H), 5.73 (s, 1H), 5.22 (s, 1H), 5.17 (s, 1H),
4.11 (d, J = 5.7 Hz, 2H), 1.66 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
169.57, 148.46, 141.36, 140.77, 136.05, 130.41, 129.44, 128.59, 128.18,
128.09, 127.63, 126.60, 115.70, 41.63, 23.04. HRMS (ESI): m/z calculated
for C17H18NO [M+H]+:252.1388 found: 252.1389.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, alternative preparation shown,
portionwise addition of NaH stage 1, dropwise addition of bromide stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Intramolecular C-N Bond Cleavage, 1,4-Migration, sp3 C-H
