$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-Methoxy-5a,6,7,9a-tetrahydro-dibenzofuran-1-carbaldehyde 56 A test tube
containing aryl ether 41 (15 mg, 0.042 mmol), palladium(II) acetate (0.5
mg, 0. 006 mmol), triphenylphosphine (2 mg, 0.008 mmol) was evacuated and
filled with argon three times. The test tube was charged with degassed
acetonitrile (0.4 mL) followed by triethyl amine (6 μL, 0.043 mmol) and
the resulting yellow solution heated at 100 ºC for 10h. The crude
reaction mixture was directly chromatographed eluting with 20% diethyl
ether: petrole um ether to afford 56 (8 mg, 82%) as a colorless film.
Characterized as a 3:1:1 mixture of 56a:56b:56c. 56a: IR (film): 3032,
2928, 2845, 2732, 1685, 1612, 1579, 1438, 1286, 1238, 1086 cm-1. 1H-NMR
(CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ 9.88 (s, 1H), 7.29 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (d, J =
8.3 Hz, 1H), 5.83 (dd, J = 10.2 and 6.3 Hz, 1H), 5.78 (dt, J = 10.2 and
3.0 Hz, 1H), 5.09 (dt, J = 7. 0 and 3.4 Hz, 1H), 4.35 (m, 1H), 3.94 (s,
3H), 2.40 (dm, J = 11.7 Hz, 1H), 2.31-2.22 (m, 1 H), 1.99 (dm, J = 17.3
HZ, 1H), 1.64 (dddd, J = 14.4, 12.2, 5.7 and 2.7 Hz, 1H). 13C-NMR (CDCl3,
125 MHz): δ 190.9, 149.6, 148.7, 134.3, 128.2, 128.1, 128.0, 125.2, 110.4
83.5, 56.1, 41.0, 24.3, 18.9. HRMS Calc'd for C14H14O3: 230.0943. Found:
23.0943. Additional signals for 56b and 56c; 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 500 MHz): δ
9.89 (s, 1H, c), 9.87 (s, 1H, b), 7.33 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1H, b), 7.30 (d, J
= 8.6 Hz, 1H, c), 6.86 (d, J = 8.5 H z, 1H, b), 6.84 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H,
c), 6.21 (m, 1H, b), 6.14 (dm, J = 10.0 Hz, 1H, b), 5.91 ( m, 1H, c),
5.15 (ddd, J = 8.6, 5.7 and 3.4 Hz, 1H, c), 4.93 (m, 1H, b), 3.97 (m, 1H,
b), 3.94 ( s, 3H, b), 3.93 (s, 3H, c), 3.75 (m, 1H, c), 2.66 (m, 1H, c),
2.55 (m, 2H, c), 2.14-2.05 (m). 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz): δ 191.0, 149.5,
149.0, 132.5, 128.6, 128.2, 126.3, 125.0, 123. 0, 110.3, 110.2, 84.0,
80.1, 56.0, 40.2, 27.7, 27.0, 24.4, 23.9.
