$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1. Electrochemically Mediated Heck Reaction 13.5 mg (0.06 mmol) Pd(OAc)2,
128.8 mg (0.4 mmol) Bu4NBr, 85.9 mg (0.3 mmol) 1-pyrenemethyl acrylate,
52.4 mg (0.2 mmol) methyl 4-iodobenzoate were dissolved in a 9:1:1
DMF/H2O/Et3N solution (11 mL). The resulting solution was sonicated under
Argon and then subjected to cathodic reduction which was carried out in a
single cell fitted with platinum cathode (2 cm2) and platinum anode (2
cm2). Electricity was supplied from the regulated DC power (5.0 mA/cm2)
until methyl 4-iodobenzoate disappeared (0.89 F/mol). 1 mol/L HCl was
added until pH<5, and then extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL×3). The CH2Cl2
fraction was washed with brine and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After
concentration, the CH2Cl2 extract was chromatographed on silica gel
eluting with Hexane/EtOAc (10:1) to afford Heck reaction product (Figure
S1) in 82% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM electrochemical, stereoselective, ultrasound
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Building Addressable Libraries: The Use of Electrochemistry for Spatially
Isolating a Heck Reaction on a Chip
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
