$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure- Mizoroki-Heck Reactions A
solution of aryl bromide (0.04 M), n-butyl acrylate (2 equiv), TEA (2
equiv), tri-tert- butylphosphonium tetrafluoroborate salt (1 equiv) and
Herrmanns palladacycle (1%) in DMF was prepared and then pumped at a flow
rate of 0.5 mL/min through the 200 mm × 3 mm ϕi SiC reactor at a
temperature of 190-210°C. The crude reaction mixture was concentrated and
thereafter subjected to silica gel column chromatography to give product.
compound: 3h, yield:82% (172 mg), a colorless liquid, reactant: 1h. 1H
NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 7.66 (d, 1H, J= 15.9 Hz), 7.50-7.47 (m, 1H),
7.35-7.31 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.28 (m, 1H), 6.26 (d, 1H, J= 15.9 Hz), 4.20 (t,
2H, J= 6.7 Hz), 1.74-1.63 (m, 2H), 1.49-1.38 (m, 2H), 0.96 (t, 3H, J =
7.4 Hz). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 167.4, 138.1, 137.7, 128.1, 127.0,
125.3, 118.1, 64.5, 30.9, 19.3, 13.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective, thermal, Mizoroki-Heck Reaction,
SiC reactor used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Safe Palladium-Catalyzed Cross-Couplings with Microwave Heating Using
Continuous-Flow Silicon Carbide Reactors
