$DATUM The following reductive Heck reaction proceeded with poor reproducibility
when standard conditions (PdCl2(CH3CN)2, HCOOH, TEA, DMF, 50 °C) were
used8 ; Acetic acid
(2R,3S)-3-cyano-2,3-dimethyl-2,3-dihydro-benzofuran-4-yl ester 14, yield
81% M.p. = 63-64 °C. IR (film): 2985, 2937, 1771, 1616, 1601, 1456, 1386,
1261, 1196, 1175, 1090, 1032, 897, 862, 737 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ: 7.26 (dd, J = 8.3 Hz, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.75 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 6.71
(d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 4.55 (q, J = 6.3 Hz, 1H), 2.38 (s, 3H), 1.73 (s,
3H), 1.63 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 168.6, 159.7,
147.5, 131.3, 118.7, 118.6, 115.7, 108.3, 87.3, 44.5, 24.2, 20.8, 17.6.
HRMS m/z C13H13NO3 (M+) Calc´d 231.0895, Found 231.0891. [α]25 D 139.7 [c
1.06, CH2Cl2]. Enantiomers were separated by HPLC on chiralcel OD eluting
with heptane/isopropanol 99:1 (1 ml/min); 2R,3S 15.73, 2S,3R 17.95.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
