$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 120-94-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Heck Couplings with Pd-
Smopex-111 in N-Methyl-2-pyrrolidione (NMP). To a N2-purged 50-mL
round-bottomed flask were added 4-bromoacetophenone (2.0 g, 10 mmol),
butyl acrylate (1.68 g, 13 mmol), N,N-diisopropylethylamine (1.68 g, 13
mmol), Pd- Smopex-111 (0.8 g , 2.5%), and N-methyl-2-pyrrolidinone (NMP,
10 mL). The resulting mixture was heated at 118 °C for 16 h, and the
reaction was monitored by HPLC. After the completion of the reaction, the
mixture was cooled to room temperature and filtered through Celite. The
filtrate was diluted with 50 mL of ethyl acetate and washed with two
10-mL portions of water. The organic layer was dried over MgSO4 and
concentrated to dryness under pressure.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, Heck reaction, Smopex 111 supported palladium
catalyst used, catalyst recycled
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Smopex-111: A new catalyst for Heck and Suzuki cross-coupling
reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jiang, Xinglong; Sclafani, Joseph; Prasad, Kapa; Repic, Oljan; Blacklock,
Thomas J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Process Research & Development (2007), 11(4), 769-772

