$DATUM Non-migration reaction conditions (procedure A): 6 The appropriate aryl
iodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol), n-Bu4NCl (0.0694 g,
0.25 mmol), NaHCO3 (0.042 g, 0.5 mmol) and ethyl acrylate (0.10 g, 1.0
mmol) in DMF (1 ml) under Ar at 100 °C were stirred for the specified
length of time. The reaction mixture was then cooled to room temperature,
diluted with diethyl ether (35 mL) and washed with brine (30 mL). The
aqueous layer was reextracted with diethyl ether (15 mL). The organic
layers were combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and the solvent removed
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
on a silica gel column. Ethyl E-3-(4’-dimethylaminobiphen-2-yl)acrylate
(2b). N,N-Dimethyl-4-(2- iodophenyl)aniline (1b) (80.8 mg, 0.25 mmol) was
allowed to react with ethyl acrylate under non-migration reaction
conditions (procedure A) for 1 d. The reaction mixture was
chromatographed using 5:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate to afford 59.0 mg (80%)
of the indicated compound as a yellow solid: mp 117-118 °C; 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.30 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 3.01 (s, 6H), 4.22 (q, J = 7.2 Hz,
2H), 6.39 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 6.78-6.80 (m, 2H), 7.20-7.22 (m, 2H),
7.31-7.40 (m, 3H), 7.66 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.84 (d, J = 16.0 Hz, 1H);
13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.4, 40.6, 60.3, 112.2, 118.5, 126.7, 126.9, 127.7,
129.8, 130.4, 130.7, 132.6, 143.2, 144.7, 150.0, 167.2; IR (CH2Cl2) 2975,
2926, 2857, 1715, 1612, 1631, 1526 cm-1; HRMS m/z 295.1580 (calcd for
C19H21NO2, 295.1572); Anal. C, 77.05, H, 7.29; N, 4.57 (calcd for
C19H21NO2: C, 77.26; H, 7.17; N, 4.77).
