$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Asymmetric Heck
Arylation of 6a and Subsequent Hydrolysis Producing 4. The reactants were
added to a reaction vial in the following order: aryl iodide or aryl
bromide 2 (0.60 mmol), enol ether 6a (0.78 mmol, 0.152 g), Pd(OAc)2
(0.018 mmol, 0.004 g), NaOAc (0.72 mmol, 0.059 g), LiCl (1.20 mmol, 0.051
g), K2CO3 (0.72 mmol, 0.100 g), DMF (2 mL) and water (0.2 mL). The tube
was closed and the contents were magnetically stirred and heated for 1-3
days at 70-100 °C (Table 1). The reaction was interrupted when GC-MS
analysis showed no further improvements in conversion. After cooling, 0.5
mL concd HCl was added and the contents stirred for 30 min. After full
hydrolysis (GC-MS) the reaction mixture was diluted with 10 mL 0.5 M HCl
and extracted five times with diethyl ether. The ethereal phases were
washed twice with 0.1 M NaOH and dried with K2CO3(s). Evaporation of the
solvent and silica column chromatography. Pure products 4.
(R)-2-(4-Benzoyl-phenyl)-2-methyl-cyclopentanone 4g Compound 4g was
obtained after silica column (hexane-diethyl ether, 90:10) in 78% yield
and 94% ee using 4-bromobenzophenone 2i as starting material; HPLC ODH
(isohexane/2-propanol 95:5) 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.81-7.74 (m, 4H),
7.61-7.55 (m, 1H) 7.51- 7.44 (m, 4H), 2.60-2.52 (m, 1H), 2.43-2.36 (m,
2H), 2.13-1.86 (m, 3H), 1.43 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 220.1,
196.3, 147.7, 137.6, 136.0, 132.5, 130.4, 130.1, 128.4, 126.4, 53.3,
38.1, 37.8, 25.0, 18.9; MS (70 eV) m/z (relative intensity) 278 (M+, 38),
145 (100), 105 (57). Anal calcd for C19H18O2: C, 82.0; H, 6.5. Found: C,
82.4; H, 6.7. tr = 29 min (+), tr = 33 min (-); flowrate = 0.5 mL/min.
[α] D 23 = +45°
