$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel.
(2S,3S)-2-ethanoyl-3-(4-methoxyphenyl)-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-1-one (6f)
Compound 6f was prepared according to the general procedure (II) using
(R,Z)-3-((2-
bromophenyl)(hydroxy)methyl)-4-(4-methoxyphenyl)but-3-en-2-one (25 mg,
0.069 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (25 μL, 0.138 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a white solid (15 mg,
77%). 90% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel OJ, 1 mL/min, 3-5% 2-propanol in
hexane tR = 11.45 (minor) and 18.92 (major) min (UV 254 nm). FTIR (film)
3472, 2970, 2904, 2859, 1628, 1463, 1431, 1363, 1271, 1254, 1114, 996
cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.09 (bs, 1H), 7.82 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H),
7.47 (ddd, J = 8.5, 8.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.38 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 0 Hz, 1H),
7.22 (dd, J = 7.5, 0.5 Hz, 1H), 7.07 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2H), 6.82 (d, J =
8.5 Hz, 2H), 4.80 (s, 1H), 3.78 (s, 3H), 1.84 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.1, 178.0, 158.5, 153.1, 136.6, 133.5, 132.9, 128.7(2C),
127.6, 125.5, 123.0, 115.7, 114.2(2C), 55.2, 47.3, 20.7 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z
calcd for [M+H]+ (C18H16O3H)+: 281 Found: [M+H]+ 281.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Substituted Indanones from Silyloxyallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Brekan, Jonathan A.; Reynolds, Troy E.; Scheidt, Karl A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(5), 1472-1473

