$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel. (6b) - Compound 6b
was prepared according to the general procedure (II) using (R,Z)-3-((6-
bromobenzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)(hydroxy)methyl)-4-phenylbut-3-en-2-one (37
mg, 0.098 mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (36 μL, 0.197 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The
crude material was purified by column chromatography (15% Ethyl
Acetate:hexanes) to give the title compound as a white solid (22 mg,
76%). 81% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel OJ, 0.5 mL/min, 10% 2-propanol in
hexane tR = 35.78 (minor) and 51.13 (major) min (UV 230 nm). FTIR (film)
3429, 2919, 1649, 1608, 1464, 1392, 1279, 1035 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 13.85 (bs, 1H), 7.32-7.24 (bm, 3H), 7.20 (s, 1H), 7.13 (dd, J =
7.0, 1.5 Hz, 2H), 6.59 (s, 1H), 6.01 (d, J = 20.0 Hz, 2H), 4.72 (s, 1H),
1.76 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 194.1, 173.2, 153.3, 150.3,
148.3, 141.2, 131.2, 128.9(2C), 127.6(2C), 127.1, 115.7, 105.4, 102.1,
102.0, 47.6, 19.7 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z calcd for [M+Na]+ (C18H14O4Na)+: 317
Found: [M+H]+ 317
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Substituted Indanones from Silyloxyallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
