$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
8-Methyl-1H-indole[1,2-b]benzo[d]isothiazole-10-(endo-norbornan-2-yl)-5,5-dioxide
(23). Compound 224 (99.3 mg, 0.25 mmol) and norbornene (25.9 mg, 0.275
mmol) were allowed to react under our standard reaction conditions for 1
d. The reaction mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (30 mL) and washed
with brine (30 mL). The organic layer was dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
the solvent removed under reduced pressure to afford 68.0 g (75 % yield)
of the indicated compound 23 as a yellow solid, which is easily
recrystallized from CHCl3/hexanes: mp 255-256 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
1.42-1.49 (m, 3H), 1.71-1.75 (m, 2H), 1.89-1.94 (m, 2H), 2.07-2.08 (m,
1H), 2.51 (br s, 4H), 2.65 (br s, 1H), 3.28-3.31 (m, 1H), 7.18-7.23 (m,
1H), 7.26-7.28 (m, 1H), 7.31-7.36 (m, 1H), 7.60 (s, 1H), 7.68-7.72 (m,
2H), 7.83 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 22.3, 29.4, 30.7, 36.5,
37.8, 37.9, 41.1, 42.7, 112.0, 122.6, 122.8, 123.0, 123.2, 123.5, 125.5,
128.7, 129.2, 132.2, 133.0, 135.5, 145.0 (one sp2 carbon missing due to
overlap); IR (neat, cm-1) 2952, 2866, 1597, 1326, 1179; HRMS Calcd for
C22H21NO2S: 363.1293. Found: 363.1300.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
