$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 0.2 mmol (1 equiv) of the enamide, 4.5 mg
(0.02 mmol, 10 mol%) of palladium (II)acetate and 10.5 mg (0.04 mmol, 20
mol%) of triphenylphosphine, Cs2CO3 ( 78.3 mg, 1.2 equiv) were dissolved
in 2mL of dry DMF in a screw cap vial under argon atmosphere. And the
vial was heated at 120 °C under the atmosphere of Ar for 24 h. The
solution was diluted by EA, washed by ammonium chloride saturated
solution. The organic layer was concentrated in vacuum and the product
was isolated through flash column chromatography (hexane/ethylacetate =
4:1) to furnish the related products.
1-(8-chloro-3-phenylisoquinolin-2(1H)-yl) ethanone 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 7.50 – 7.41 (m, 2H), 7.36 – 7.29 (m, 3H), 7.17 (dd, J = 8.0,
1.3 Hz, 1H), 7.11 (t, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.05 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 6.49 (s,
1H), 5.12 (s, 2H), 1.55 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 171.47,
141.05, 137.54, 134.22, 131.36, 131.12, 129.17, 129.01, 128.40, 128.33,
126.40, 123.78, 117.22, 43.51, 24.38. HRMS (ESI): m/z calculated for
C17H15NOCl [M+H]+:284.0842 found:284.0841.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, regioselective, product depends on ligand and base, Heck
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Intramolecular C-N Bond Cleavage, 1,4-Migration, sp3 C-H
Activation, and Heck Reaction: Four Controllable Diverse Pathways
Depending on the Judicious Choice of the Base and Ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Min; Zhang, Xiang; Zhuang, Yu-Xuan; Xu, Yun-He; Loh, Teck-Peng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
