$DATUM rac-cis-9-Acetyl-6,8-dimethyl-2,4a,9,9a-tetrahydro-1H-carbazol-3-yl
acetate (32): In a sealable pressure tube were placed a stir bar,
anti-27t (0.092 g, 0.250 mmol), Pd2(dba)3.CHCl3 (0.013 g, 0.0125 mmol),
and P(o-tol)3 (0.017 g, 0.055 mmol). A degassed 10:1 MeCN:H2O solvent
mixture (2.5 mL) was added, followed by Me2NBu (0.063 g, 0.625 mmol). The
tube was sealed, heated at 80 °C for 1 h, and recooled to room
temperature. Saturated aqueous NH4Cl (5 mL) was added, and the mixture
was extracted with EtOAc (3 x 5 mL). The combined organic layers were
washed with brine (1 x 10 mL), dried over MgSO4, filtered, and
concentrated by rotary evaporation. Column chromatography (1:1
hexanes:EtOAc) provided an inseparable mixture (63 mg total) of the title
compound (0.054 g, 0.182 mmol, 73%) and tri(o-tolyl)phosphine oxide8
(0.009 g, 0.027 mmol). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.86 (s, 1H), 6.79 (s,
1H), 5.76 (dd, J = 4.8 Hz, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 4.53 (br s, 1H), 4.06 (br m, 1H),
2.58-2.43 (m, 1H), 2.28 (s, 3H), 2.26 (s, 3H), 2.22 (s, 3H), 2.14 (s,
3H), 2.08-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.70 (dq, J = 12.6 Hz, 4.5 Hz, 1H); HRMS (EI)
calcd for C18H21NNaO3 [M + Na]+: 322.1419, found: 322.1440.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Heck reaction, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
