$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
(3E)-4-(4,4-Dimethyl-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-5-yl)but-3-en-2-one (26).
Compound 24 (68.5 mg, 0.25 mmol) and methyl vinyl ketone (0.375 mmol)
were allowed to react under our standard reaction conditions for 18 h.
The reaction mixture was diluted with diethyl ether (30 mL) and washed
with brine (30 mL). The organic layer was dried (Na2SO4), filtered and
the solvent removed under reduced pressure. The residue was
chromatographed (3:1 hexane/EtOAc) to afford 42.0 mg of the indicated
compound (73 % yield) as a yellow oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.47 (s, 6H),
1.85 (t, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H), 2.38 (s, 3H), 4.15 (t, J = 5.2 Hz, 2H), 6.47
(d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (dd, J = 0.9, 6.0 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (dd, J = 1.2,
5.7 Hz, 1H), 7.09 (t, J = 5.7 Hz, 1H), 8.17 (d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 28.2, 30.5, 31.6, 41.1, 62.5, 119.8, 121.6, 127.5, 128.3,
130.1, 135.9, 144.8, 154.7, 198.3; IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 3020, 2964, 1705;
HRMS Calcd for C15H18O2: 230.1307. Found: 230.1311.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Heck reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Alkyl to Aryl Migration and Cyclization: An Efficient
Synthesis of Fused Polycycles via Multiple C-H Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
